## Tips {% #tips %}

{% aside type="tip" id="towers-start-with-one" %}
Turn on one kingdom first and watch the [logs](/war-room/logs/) for an hour. When its attacks look right, turn on the next kingdom.
{% /aside %}

- A small **Search radius** finds fewer towers, but the marches are short.
- **Widen search when nothing is found** is off by default. When a scan finds no tower, it widens the radius by 10 {% term id="click" %}clicks{% /term %}, up to 100, and scans again within a few minutes. When towers are in the nearer range again, it narrows back a step at each scan, down to your **Search radius**. The status says when the search is widened.
- Set **Most attacks a day** for each kingdom, so one kingdom cannot use up the account's whole daily cap.
- Towers has no **Log only** setting. To test, start with one kingdom and a low **Most attacks a day**.

## Related errors {% #errors %}

- [TOO_MANY_ATTACK_PLUGINS](/errors/#too-many-attack-plugins): more attack plugins are on than your cap allows, so the bot does not start.
- [PLUGIN_ATTACK_CAP](/errors/#plugin-attack-cap): the settings do not save because too many attack plugins are on.
- [PLUGIN_OPTION_CASTLE](/errors/#plugin-option-castle): **Castle to attack from** names a castle the account no longer has.
- [PLUGIN_OPTION_ARMY](/errors/#plugin-option-army): the army setting can't be read.
- [CASTLE_LOCKED](/errors/#castle-locked): Alert and autostation is moving the castle's troops, so no attack leaves it for now.
